From: Saphira packaging <recipes@saphira.vm2.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] musl: deactivate kernel struct ethhdr in os_vif_linux

musl <netinet/if_ether.h> (via common/netaddr.h) and kernel UAPI
<linux/if_ether.h> (via <linux/if_tun.h>) both define struct ethhdr
with no mutual guard. The kernel header honors __UAPI_DEF_ETHHDR=0
(its documented libc mechanism): keep the libc copy, which also
carries the ether_* declarations. This TU only needs TUN ioctls,
never struct ethhdr.

--- a/src-plugins/subsystems/os_linux/os_vif_linux.c
+++ b/src-plugins/subsystems/os_linux/os_vif_linux.c
@@ -47,2 +47,9 @@
 #include <fcntl.h>
+/* musl <netinet/if_ether.h> (via common/netaddr.h) and kernel UAPI
+ * <linux/if_ether.h> (via <linux/if_tun.h>) both define struct ethhdr
+ * with no mutual guard. The kernel header honors __UAPI_DEF_ETHHDR=0
+ * (its documented libc mechanism): keep the libc copy. This TU only
+ * needs TUN ioctls, never struct ethhdr.
+ */
+#define __UAPI_DEF_ETHHDR 0
 #include <linux/if_tun.h>
